## Add live activity log to ontology wizard spinner

Context: During AI ontology generation the wizard overlay only showed the latest
status line. Agent `on_step` messages were logged server-side but overwritten on
each poll, so users could not follow the process. This adds a structured step
checklist and a scrollable activity trace on the spinner page.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/task_manager/models.py
   Add `TaskLogEntry` and `log_entries` on `Task`; expose via `to_dict()`.
2. src/back/core/task_manager/TaskManager.py
   Append deduplicated log lines in `start_task`, `update_progress`, `advance_step`,
   `complete_task`, and `fail_task` (skip `__iter__:` refinement payloads).
3. src/api/routers/internal/ontology.py
   Advance wizard task steps through init → gather → generate before the agent runs.
4. src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-wizard.js
   Render step checklist + activity log during polling; wire `renderAgentStepsLog`
   on completion.
5. src/front/static/global/css/components.css
   Widen overlay and style scrollable activity log panel.
6. tests/units/core/test_task_manager.py
   Cover log accumulation, deduplication, and `__iter__:` filtering.

Modified files:
- src/back/core/task_manager/models.py
- src/back/core/task_manager/TaskManager.py
- src/back/core/task_manager/__init__.py
- src/api/routers/internal/ontology.py
- src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-wizard.js
- src/front/static/global/css/components.css
- tests/units/core/test_task_manager.py

Tests: uv run pytest -q -m "not scenario" → 3137 passed, 275 skipped, 5 deselected in 25.12s

## Apply task progress overlay to Batch Auto-Map page

Context: The ontology wizard now shows a branded spinner with step checklist and
activity log during async work. The Batch Auto-Map page still used a minimal inline
progress bar with only the latest message. This reuses the same overlay pattern so
users can follow auto-map agent steps live.

Changes:

1. src/front/static/global/js/task-progress-ui.js
   Extract shared overlay builder, step checklist, activity log, and agent-steps
   panel used by wizard and auto-map.
2. src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-wizard.js
   Delegate to `TaskProgressUI` instead of inline render helpers.
3. src/front/static/mapping/js/mapping-autoassign.js
   Full-page overlay on `#autoassign-section` with step log + activity trace;
   live gauge updates preserved during polling.
4. src/front/templates/partials/mapping/_mapping_autoassign.html
   Remove legacy inline progress card (overlay is JS-driven).
5. src/front/templates/mapping.html, src/front/templates/ontology.html
   Load `task-progress-ui.js` before wizard/auto-map modules.
6. src/front/static/global/css/components.css
   Generalize overlay styles to `.task-progress-*` (wizard aliases kept).
7. src/api/routers/internal/mapping.py, src/back/objects/mapping/Mapping.py
   Align auto-map task steps with init → prepare → agent → finalize and advance
   through them during the background run.

Modified files:
- src/front/static/global/js/task-progress-ui.js
- src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-wizard.js
- src/front/static/mapping/js/mapping-autoassign.js
